> There should be no unsafe scripts in the code. Is there any solution to reproduce your case?

It can be triggered when the reverse proxy nginx contains the following security content, and all chat requests sent to the server are intercepted locally by the browser:
security.conf
`# security headers
add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
add_header Referrer-Policy "no-referrer-when-downgrade" always;
add_header Content-Security-Policy "default-src 'self' http: https: ws: wss: data: blob: 'unsafe-inline'; frame-ancestors 'self';" always;
add_header Permissions-Policy "interest-cohort=()" always;
add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains" always;

# .files
location ~ /\.(?!well-known) {
    deny all;
}
`
In addition, the above content is the content of the security configuration file generated by the nginxconfig.io website by default. I fixed the problem after commenting out the import of that config file.

